abstract: >-
  The Sustainable Digital Architecture Framework (SDAF) is an open,
  structured methodology for integrating sustainability into the design,
  evaluation, governance and assurance of digital systems. It establishes
  a five-phase assessment lifecycle and requirements for measurement,
  evidence quality, uncertainty, traceability, decision-making, lifecycle
  impacts, circularity, governance, enterprise adoption and ecosystem
  interoperability.
